# Milestone: M3
# Covers: assertion error regression in Semaphore caused by '|' implementation
#         bug; s.release(), s.acquire() across pipe separator must not assert.
# deferred: v1.x — Semaphore stdlib type not in v1.0 scope
# matrix-row: stdlib-semaphore
#
# Reason:
#   This is a Semaphore regression test — Semaphore is a stdlib type scheduled
#   for M6.  The underlying bug (assertion in Semaphore due to '|' implementation)
#   is a legacy 2.x kernel issue; our M6 implementation will be written from
#   scratch and will not carry that specific bug forward.  The fixture is preserved
#   for reference and will be activated when Semaphore lands in M6.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Semaphore type):
# # var s = Semaphore.new(0) | {};
# # s.release(), s.acquire();
